# Cardan gears: a wheel of radius r inside a ring of radius 2r, and the
# straight line that falls out of it.
#
#   centre --HINGE z-- crank --HINGE z-- planet        ring: reference only
#
# When a wheel rolls inside a ring of exactly twice its radius, every
# point on the wheel's rim travels along a straight line — a diameter of
# the ring. It is the Tusi couple, and it is the reason Cardan gears
# were used to convert rotation into straight-line motion before the
# slider-crank was common. The hypocycloid of ratio 2 is degenerate: it
# is not an approximation to a straight line, it IS one.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE BELIEVING THE PICTURE. There is no rolling contact
# here. This joint set has four constraints — CONSTRAIN (1 row), BALL
# (3), UNIVERSAL (4), HINGE (5) — and not one of them couples a rotation
# to a translation, which is what rolling means. There is no gear
# constraint and no line constraint either.
#
# So the outer ring is drawn for reference and NOTHING is attached to
# it. It is a static body, present only to show the circle the planet
# would be rolling inside. The planet is not touching it in any sense
# the solver knows about.
#
# What holds the 2:1 relation is the START, not a constraint:
#
#     crank  angular_velocity = [0, 0,  1]
#     planet angular_velocity = [0, 0, -1]
#
# For a wheel rolling inside a ring of twice its radius the wheel turns
# once backwards for each forward turn of the crank, so equal and
# opposite rates ARE the rolling condition. And with no gravity and no
# torque anywhere, both rates are conserved: the crank's because the
# planet's reaction on it is purely centripetal, and the planet's
# because its centre of mass sits exactly ON the hinge, so the force
# there has no moment about it. The ratio therefore persists, and the
# rim point runs along the x axis.
#
# THE DIFFERENCE THIS MAKES IS MEASURABLE, and it is the point of the
# recording. A real gear pair would hold the line however it were
# loaded. Here the ratio is only an initial condition, so integration
# error accumulates in it and the line slowly degrades:
#
#     315 cold restarts, one per frame   |y| <= 1.795e-3
#     the same 6.3 s run continuously    |y| <= 4.137e-5
#
# a factor of 43, and the same restart-versus-continuation effect as the
# rod chain (grammar §12.9). The straight line is exact in the geometry;
# what you see is what one floored tolerance and 315 restarts leave of
# it. Watch the trail: it is a line, and it is 2 units long, exactly
# 2r either side of the centre.
set system.g_constant = 0
set system.uniform_gravity = [0, 0, 0]
collide off
# Every joint pivots at the MIDPOINT of its pair, so the anchor sits one
# crank-radius the far side of the centre, and the crank and planet
# share a centre: that puts the first pivot on the origin and the second
# exactly on the planet's axle at [0.5, 0, 0].
new point as centre { mass = 1, position = [-0.5, 0, 0], inverse_mass = 0 }
new cuboid as crank { mass = 0.3, half_extents = [0.5, 0.04, 0.02], position = [0.5, 0, 0] }
# The planet is a cylinder, symmetric about its LOCAL z, hinged about z:
# here that IS correct, because a gear wheel turns about its own axis.
new cylinder as planet { mass = 1, radius = 0.5, half_height = 0.03, position = [0.5, 0, 0] }
# Reference only — no joint attaches to this.
new torus as ring { mass = 1, ring_radius = 1.0, tube_radius = 0.02, position = [0, 0, 0], inverse_mass = 0 }
hinge centre crank [0, 0, 1]
hinge crank planet [0, 0, 1]
method ida
# Consistent by construction: each body's material point at its pivot has
# the velocity the other gives it, so g_dot = J u = 0 to roundoff.
set crank.angular_velocity = [0, 0, 1]
set crank.velocity = [0, 0.5, 0]
set planet.angular_velocity = [0, 0, -1]
set planet.velocity = [0, 0.5, 0]
